From 9a032e1c151cb3799cfa064d2af026f742b10a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:41:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Take class names from typeid portably

ASMTItem::classname(), Item::classname(), the printOn() methods and the
time series labels cut a fixed number of characters off typeid(...).name(),
which only works for MSVC's 'class MbD::X'. GCC and Clang give the mangled
'N3MbD19ASMTRackPinionJointE', so the ASMT export on Linux and macOS wrote
joint types like 'PinionJointE'. plainClassName() demangles and strips the
namespace; the result on Windows is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OndselSolver/ASMTItem.cpp   |  5 ++---
 OndselSolver/ASMTJoint.cpp  |  5 +++--
 OndselSolver/CMakeLists.txt |  1 +
 OndselSolver/Item.cpp       |  9 +++-----
 OndselSolver/Symbolic.cpp   |  5 ++---
 OndselSolver/TypeName.h     | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 OndselSolver/TypeName.h

